card.statement:
The quotient map $\pi_{\mf l}:\,\mc V(\mf p)\twoheadrightarrow\mc V(\mf g^f)$ restricts to a differential algebra isomorphism $\pi_{\mf l}:\,\mc W_{\mf l}\stackrel{\sim}{\longrightarrow}\mc V(\mf g^f)$, and the inverse map $\pi_{\mf l}^{-1}:\,\mc V(\mf g^f)\stackrel{\sim}{\longrightarrow}\mc W_{\mf l}$ is defined on generators by

$$
\begin{array}{l}
\displaystyle{
\vphantom{\Big(}
\pi_{\mf l}^{-1}(a)=\varphi_{\mf l}(a)
\,\,\,\, \text{ for } a\in\mf g_0^f
\,,} \\
\displaystyle{
\vphantom{\Big(}
\pi_{\mf l}^{-1}(u)=\psi_{\mf l}(u)
\,\,\,\, \text{ for } u\in\mf g_{-\frac12}
\,,} \\
\displaystyle{
\pi_{\mf l}^{-1}(f)=L_{\mf l}-\frac12\sum_{i\in J_0^f}\varphi_{\mf l}(a_i)\varphi_{\mf l}(a^i)
=:\tilde{L}_{\mf l}
\,.}
\end{array}
$$
